  "bibliography": {
    "abstract": "This study examined how planned street-design changes for safer cycling are perceived when visualized through a dynamic 3D model versus static 2D plan. We assessed who experiences difficulties interpreting 2D plans, compared perceived safety and appeal across three visualizations (current street video, 2D plan and 3D model), and tested whether 2D plan interpretation difficulties affected perceptions. In a web-based survey of 417 adults, women and younger participants reported more difficulties with the 2D plan. The future design in 3D was perceived as safer and more appealing than the 2D plan, especially in those with difficulties to interpret the 2D plan.",
